************************************************************************	Window Manager Version 3.2**          Copyright Apple Computer, Inc. 1986-1992*          All rights reserved*          Written by Dan Oliver** Change History** 08/20/87 	Dan** Start ROMing.** 26 Jun 88	Harry Yee** Converted to MAX** 27 Jan 88	Steven Glass** Removed Pop routines and used shared routines in WCM library.* Used shared PushDPage routine in WCM library.* Changed name of SetOrigin to SetTheOrigin to avoid naming conflict with *   QuickDraw.** 29 Jun 88	Steven Glass** Made WindDragRect public so that we can have control manager* link to it in ROM.  (CtlStartup was getting address and patching* call table.  This does not work in ROM so we must have right value* in place to start with.)** 14 JUL 88	Dan Oliver** Changed TaskScroll routine so that it would not pass a negative X origin to new_origin.  The* problem seems to be that a window's origin may not match the scroll bar values when the origin* is being masked to a grid.  This is OK as long as the move deltas (as in this case) don't get* out of range.  The top end of the range is checked in new_origin, the bottom is now checked in* TaskScroll.** 23 Jul 88	Steven Glass** Changed CheckUpdate, TrackGoAway and TrackZoom so that when they* return TRUE, all the bits in the returned word are set.  A problem has* occured for developers using high level languages:  The language test* for TRUE was not always working.  Pascal looks in bit 0, C looks in * bit 15.  By setting all the bits, it might work.** 10 Aug 88	Dan Oliver** Free allocated data area on shutdown.** 20 Oct 88	Dan O.** Added CompileString to function table.* Added Window Manager error code equates.** 21 Oct 88	Dan O.** Changed airport & calc_vis routines to limit the window that have their visRgn recomputed* when a window is brought to the top.  Now visRgns for windows behind the window being brought* foreward are not recomputed.** DragRect changed to draw 4 lines rather than 1 RECT.  This keeps the cursor from blinking off* and on in some cases.*** 24 Oct 88	Dan O.** Window Manager nows looks for DeskMessage (defined in Message Center documentation) to determine* what to draw for the desktop.  The Window Manager does not look for the message each time, rather* it is set by a Desktop call.** Added an operation number FindDeskPatt (8) added to Desktop call.  No additional parameter * passed and no parameter returned.  This operation makes the Window Manager check the Message* Center for a DeskMessage it can use to draw the desktop image.  If a message is found it will* be used when drawing the desktop in the future.  This call will not redraw the desktop.** WindStartup and WindNewRes make the above call to Desktop to log in any new desktop patterns.*** 10/28/88	Dan O.** Added NewWindow2 call.* Window Manager can now handle titles as handles.  If high bit set in title pointer it's a handle.* Remove break from PaintDesk.** 07 Dec 88	Steven Glass** Added check to DeskTop and RefreshDesktop to see if the window* manager is active.  These calls are special since they are* made by the menu manager.  In the past, the menu manager could* be used without the window manager.  When this occured, the window* manager was not loaded and these calls generated dispatcher* errors.  The check just added simulates dispatcher errors* to keep the menu manager from crashing.** 14 Dec 88	Mensch** Modified NewWindw2 call so that it would conform to new toolbox verb/reference* conventions. This required the addition of an extra parameter to be passed to* the NewWindow2 call as well as a new parameter for the window template itself.* NewWindow2 will now accept a pointer/handle/or resourceID as input for the template* specifier.  In addition, the title, colortable, and control list fields can now also* take pointers and handles.** 1 Jan 89	Mensch** Changed DragWindow so that it does not call ReadMouse.  This was done to allow* journaling of clicks in a window's title bar.** 9 Jan 89	Konstantin** Added ErrorWindow call.*** 2 Mar 89	Dave Good** Rewrote SelectWindow to not use the airport routine unless either the* window that was selected or the previous topmost window was invisible.* Also changed DragWindow to not call MoveWindow unless it was actually* moved.** 28 Mar 89	Steven Glass** Removed some unimportant commented out lines left over from APW.*** 09 Apr 89	Steven Glass** Changed CkButton where it sees if mouse is really down while we are waiting* it to come up.  It was possible for MouseUp event to be left in the queue.*** 19 Apr 89	David Good** Fixed bug in SelectWindow*** 26 Apr 89	David Good** Fixed bug in EraseWindow (called by CloseWindow). If the WindGlobal* flag said to NOT change the hilighting on windows, CloseWindow used to* skip drawing. Now it just skips the hilighting, but it still draws the* frame.** 5/10/89	Mensch* Fixed bug in GetFrameColor, it was not dereferencing the handle if the* frame color table is stored in a handle.** 5/11/89	Mensch* Patched GetWRefCon so that it would not trash window manager temp storage.* This was do in order to make List Plus still compatible.** 20-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** Version is $8303.** 21-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** Fixed ErrorWindow to return with the carry set appropriately* (was always set before).** Fixed window defproc not to draw titles outside the window for* extremely narrow windows.** 24-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** Modified WindStatus to return SEC/A=0 if there are any pending* BeginUpdates.  This indicates it isn't safe to create any new* windows (and it'll make the OS use a text alert instead of an* AlertWindow call).  Added WindowUpdateCount word, and modified* BeginUpdate and EndUpdate to increment and decrement it.* (WindowUpdateCount is inline currently--not ROMmable.)** 26-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** Put back all.macros.** 26-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Added code at beginning and end of GrowWindow to preserve the* zoomRect and wFrame in case the window doesn't change size at all.** 19-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Adding new call $630E GetAuxWindInfo to return a pointer to the* auxiliary window info record for a window.  I'm going to put several* very cool tidbits of information about windows in there.** Adding new calls DoModalWindow, MWGetCtlPart, MWSetMenuProc,* MWStdDrawProc, MWSetUpEditMenu, FindCursorCtl.** 21-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** GetAuxWindInfo seems to be working.  WindShutDown disposes of the* handle if it exists.  CloseWindow calls KillAuxInfoRecord for the* window being closed.** [See NewCalls.asm for more comments.]** 5-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Added new ResizeInfoBar call for Andy N to use in the Finder.* Code is in NewCalls.asm.** 25-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Fixed bug in FindWindow where it was returning a window pointer,* instead of NIL, when it reported that the point was in the menu* bar.** 12-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Add HandleDiskInsert to call table (code in NewCalls.asm).* In WindStartUp, add call to HandleDiskInsert(1,0) to initialize.** 15-May-91	Dave Lyons** Fixed GetWKind/GetSysWFlag(NIL) to always return False.** 20-May-91	Dave Lyons** Made WindStartUp try to load and start QDAux if it isn't* already started, so that AlertWindow can use DrawIcon.** 16-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** Made WindStartUp prelocate the 320 and 640 disk-swap icons* so AlertWindow can avoid a reentrant call to LoadResource.** 12-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** Made Desktop(8) call SendRequest systemSaysNewDeskMsg (8).* Desktop operations 5 and 8 now free the WM's old copy of* the desk message, if it changes.** 5-Feb-92	Dave Lyons** Version $0303 for 6.0 final.************************************************************************* 6-Mar-92	Dave Lyons** Version $8304 for 6.1d2.** Adding new call UpdateWindow.** 1-Apr-93	Steve Stephenson** Version $0304 for 6.0.1 final.***********************************************************************	Blanks off	String asis	include 'all.macros'	include 'e16.control'	include 'WindMgrEquates.asm'	include '::ToolPatch:ToolPatchEquates.asm'	include 'e16.event'	MACRO	PushAX	phx	pha	MEND	MACRO	stax &addr,&regs	IF &addr[1:1]='[' THEN	  IF &regs='y' THEN	    sta  &addr,y	    iny	    iny	    txa	    sta  &addr,y	  ELSE	    ldy  #&regs	    sta  &addr,y	    txa	    ldy  #&regs+2	    sta  &addr,y	  ENDIF	ELSEIF &regs='s' THEN	  sta  &addr,s	  txa	  sta  &addr+2,s	ELSEIF &regs='' THEN	  sta  &addr	  stx  &addr+2	ELSE	  sta  &addr,&offset	  txa	  sta  &addr+2,&offset	ENDIF	MEND	MACRO	ldax &addr,&regs	IF &addr[1:1]='#' THEN	  lda  #&addr[2:255]	  ldx  #&addr[2:255]>>16	ELSEIF &addr[1:1]='[' THEN	  IF &regs='y' THEN	    lda  &addr,y	    pha	    iny	    iny	    lda  &addr,y	    tax	    pla	  ELSE	    ldy  #&regs+2	    lda  &addr,y	    tax	    ldy  #&regs	    lda  &addr,y	  ENDIF	ELSEIF &regs='s' THEN	  lda  &addr+2,s	  tax	  lda  &addr,s	ELSEIF &regs='' THEN	  lda  &addr	  ldx  &addr+2	ELSE	  lda  &addr+2,&offset	  pha	  lda  &addr,&offset	  plx	ENDIF	MEND	MACRO	ble &A	blt  &A	beq  &A	MEND	MACRO	bgt &A	beq  @dontTake	bge  &A@dontTake	MEND	MACRO	bcsl &A	bcc  @dontTake	brl  &A@dontTake	MEND	MACRO	bccl &A	bcs  @dontTake	brl  &A@dontTake	MEND	MACRO	beql &A	bne  @dontTake	brl  &A@dontTake	MEND	MACRO	bnel &A	beq  @dontTake	brl  &A@dontTake	MEND	MACRO	bltl &A	bge  @dontTake	brl  &A@dontTake	MEND	MACRO	bgel &A	blt  @dontTake	brl  &A@dontTake	MEND	MACRO	bmil &A	bpl  @dontTake	brl  &A@dontTake	MEND	MACRO	bpll &A	bmi  @dontTake	brl  &A@dontTake	MEND	MACRO	blel &A	blt  @takeBranch	bne  @dontTake@takeBranch	brl  &A@dontTake	MEND	MACRO	bgtl &A	blt  @dontTake	beq  @dontTake	brl  &A@dontTake	MEND;-------------------------------------------